module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FilteredCardIndex.Basic
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.FiniteTypeChartSections
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.Limits.FiniteTypeSubalgebraColimit
public import
  StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.Limits.QuasicoherentAlgebraFinitePresentationColimit
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.SmallEtaleModelCoveringSet

/-!
# An integral quasi-coherent algebra as a colimit of finite algebras of finite presentation

Let `𝒜` be an integral quasi-coherent algebra on a quasi-compact algebraic space `X`, and let
`φ` present the underlying module of `𝒜` as a filtered colimit of modules `F_k` of finite
presentation.  The system `(k, E) ↦ Sym(F_k)/(E)` of
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.Limits.QuasicoherentAlgebraFinitePresentationColimit`, with
`E` running through the finite type quasi-coherent submodules of the kernel `J_k` of
`Sym(F_k) ⟶ 𝒜`, has colimit `𝒜` and members of finite presentation.  This file shows that its
**finite** members are cofinal, so that `𝒜` is a directed colimit of quasi-coherent algebras that
are finite and of finite presentation; this is the argument the proof of Stacks 082C borrows from
the proof of Stacks 086Z ("the algebras `𝒜_{ik}` are finite for `k` large enough").

## Main results

* `SymmetricAlgebra.isIntegral_comp_algebraMap_of_surjective`: a quotient of a symmetric algebra
  in which the images of a generating set of the module are integral is integral.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.AlgebraSheaf.isFinite_of_coversTop`: a quasi-coherent algebra is
  finite as soon as it is finite over the members of a family of affine étale charts covering the
  site.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.FPAlgColim.exists_le_isFinite` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.FPAlgColim.exists_hom_isFinite`: **every member of the system maps to a
  finite one**, with the same `k`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_directed_isColimit_isFinite_isFinitePresentation_of_presentation`:
  an integral quasi-coherent algebra on a quasi-compact algebraic space is a directed colimit of
  quasi-coherent algebras that are finite and of finite presentation, given a filtered
  presentation of its underlying module by modules of finite presentation and the colimit
  assertion of Stacks 0829.
* `isFiltered_isColimit_finiteSubalgebra_and_exists_directed_finite_of_presentation`:
  both clauses of Stacks 082C on a quasi-compact and quasi-separated algebraic space whose
  quasi-coherent modules are filtered colimits of modules of finite presentation.

## Implementation notes

Finiteness of `Sym(F_k)/(E)` is checked on one affine étale chart `U` covering the site and then
spread to every affine chart by faithfully flat descent of the finiteness of the module of
sections, `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.module_finite_sections_of_coversTop`.  On `U`, the sections of
`F_k` are generated by finitely many `f₁, …, f_m`; the images of the `f_j` in `𝒜(U)` are integral,
so each `f_j` satisfies a monic equation modulo `J_k(U)`, and the value of that equation lies in a
finite type quasi-coherent submodule `E_j` of `J_k` by the colimit assertion of Stacks 0829.  Any
`E` containing the `E_j` makes `Sym(F_k)/(E)` integral over `U`, hence finite there, finite
presentation giving finite type.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 082C](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/082C)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 086Z](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/086Z)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0829](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0829)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite

universe u

namespace SymmetricAlgebra

/-- **A quotient of a symmetric algebra in which the images of a generating set of the module
are integral is integral.**  The elements of `Sym_R(M)` whose image is integral form a
subalgebra, which contains the image of `M` because the integral closure is an `R`-submodule
and `M` is spanned by the given set. -/
theorem isIntegral_comp_algebraMap_of_surjective {R M Q : Type*} [CommRing R] [AddCommGroup M]
    [Module R M] [CommRing Q] (θ : SymmetricAlgebra R M →+* Q) (hθ : Function.Surjective θ)
    (s : Set M) (hs : Submodule.span R s = ⊤)
    (hint : ∀ m ∈ s,
      (θ.comp (algebraMap R (SymmetricAlgebra R M))).IsIntegralElem (θ (ι R M m))) :
    (θ.comp (algebraMap R (SymmetricAlgebra R M))).IsIntegral := by
  let : Algebra R Q := (θ.comp (algebraMap R (SymmetricAlgebra R M))).toAlgebra
  let θ' : SymmetricAlgebra R M →ₐ[R] Q := { θ with commutes' := fun _ => rfl }
  have hM : ∀ m : M, IsIntegral R (θ (ι R M m)) := by
    have hle : Submodule.span R s ≤
        (integralClosure R Q).toSubmodule.comap (θ'.toLinearMap ∘ₗ ι R M) :=
      Submodule.span_le.2 fun m hm => hint m hm
    intro m
    exact hle (hs ▸ Submodule.mem_top)
  have hall : ∀ x : SymmetricAlgebra R M, IsIntegral R (θ x) := by
    intro x
    induction x using SymmetricAlgebra.induction with
    | algebraMap r => exact isIntegral_algebraMap
    | ι m => exact hM m
    | mul a b ha hb => rw [map_mul]; exact ha.mul hb
    | add a b ha hb => rw [map_add]; exact ha.add hb
  intro y
  obtain ⟨x, rfl⟩ := hθ y
  exact hall x

end SymmetricAlgebra

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Space

variable {B : BigFppfSite.{u}} {S : Scheme.{u}} {hS : B.Contains S}
  {F : (BigFppfOver B S hS)ᵒᵖ ⥤ Type u} {hF : IsAlgebraicSpace B S hS F}

namespace AlgebraSheaf

/-- The structure-algebra map of an algebra sheaf over a chart is finite exactly when the
sections of its underlying module there form a finite module over the chart ring. -/
theorem finite_algebraMap_iff_module_finite (A : AlgebraSheaf.{u, u} B S hS F hF)
    (U : SmallEtale B S hS F) :
    RingHom.Finite (A.algebraMap (op U)) ↔
      Module.Finite (chartRing B S hS F hF U) ((underlyingModule A).val.obj (op U)) :=
  Iff.rfl

/-- **A quasi-coherent algebra is finite as soon as it is finite over the members of a family of
affine étale charts covering the site.**  Finiteness of the sections of the underlying module
descends along a jointly faithfully flat finite family of affine charts each of which maps to a
member of the family, by `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.module_finite_sections_of_coversTop`. -/
theorem isFinite_of_coversTop {A : AlgebraSheaf.{u, u} B S hS F hF} (hA : A.IsQuasicoherent)
    {ι : Type*} {Y : ι → SmallEtale B S hS F}
    (hY : ∀ i, IsAffine ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS F ⋙ BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj (Y i)))
    (hcov : (SmallEtale.topology B S hS F).CoversTop Y)
    (hfin : ∀ i, RingHom.Finite (A.algebraMap (op (Y i)))) : A.IsFinite := fun V hV =>
  (finite_algebraMap_iff_module_finite A V).2 <|
    module_finite_sections_of_coversTop (underlyingModule A)
      (isCartesianOnAffineCharts_of_isQuasicoherentOnSite B S hS F hF _ hA) hY hcov
      (fun i => (finite_algebraMap_iff_module_finite A (Y i)).1 (hfin i)) V hV

end AlgebraSheaf

namespace FPAlgColim

variable {𝒜 : AlgebraSheaf.{u, u} B S hS F hF} {K : Type u} [SmallCategory K]
  {D : K ⥤ Modules.{u, u} B S hS F hF}
  {φ : D ⟶ (Functor.const K).obj (AlgebraSheaf.underlyingModule 𝒜)}

/-- Modules of finite presentation are quasi-coherent and of finite presentation on the site. -/
private theorem isQuasicoherentOnSite_and_isFinitePresentationOnSite
    (hfp : ∀ k, (D.obj k).IsFinitePresentation) :
    (∀ k, (D.obj k).IsQuasicoherentOnSite) ∧
      ∀ k, SheafOfModules.IsFinitePresentationOnSite (D.obj k) :=
  ⟨fun k =>
    have := hfp k
    Stacks.SheafOfModules.isQuasicoherentOnSite_of_isFinitePresentation (D.obj k),
  fun k => SheafOfModules.isFinitePresentationOnSite_of_isFinitePresentation (D.obj k) (h := hfp k)⟩

/-- **Every member of the system `(k, E) ↦ Sym(F_k)/(E)` lies under a finite one with the same
`k`.**  Here `𝒜` is an integral quasi-coherent algebra and `U` an affine étale chart covering the
site.

The sections of `F_k` over `U` are generated by finitely many `m`; the image of `m` in `𝒜(U)` is
integral, so a monic polynomial `p` sends `m` into the kernel `J_k(U)`, and that value lies in a
finite type quasi-coherent submodule `E_m` of `J_k` by the colimit assertion of Stacks 0829.  An
upper bound `E'` of `E` and the `E_m` in the filtered category of finite type quasi-coherent
submodules of `J_k` makes `Sym(F_k)/(E')` integral over `U`; finite presentation gives finite type,
so it is finite over `U`, and hence over every affine chart. -/
theorem exists_le_isFinite (hfp : ∀ k, (D.obj k).IsFinitePresentation)
    (h𝒜 : 𝒜.IsQuasicoherent) (hint : 𝒜.IsIntegral)
    (h0829 : ∀ G : Modules.{u, u} B S hS F hF, G.IsQuasicoherentOnSite →
      Nonempty (IsColimit (finiteTypeQuasicoherentSubobjectCocone B S hS F hF G)))
    {U : SmallEtale B S hS F}
    (hU : IsAffine ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS F ⋙ BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj U))
    (hcov : (SmallEtale.topology B S hS F).CoversTop fun _ : PUnit.{u + 2} => U)
    (k : K) (E₀ : FiniteTypeQuasicoherentSubobject B S hS F hF (J φ k)) :
    ∃ (E : FiniteTypeQuasicoherentSubobject B S hS F hF (J φ k)) (_ : E₀ ⟶ E),
      ((diagram φ).obj ⟨k, E⟩).IsFinite := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨hD, hD'⟩ := isQuasicoherentOnSite_and_isFinitePresentationOnSite hfp
  have hJq := isQuasicoherentOnSite_J φ hD h𝒜 k
  have hJ : IsFiltered (FiniteTypeQuasicoherentSubobject B S hS F hF (J φ k)) :=
    isFiltered_finiteTypeQuasicoherentSubobject B S hS F hF (J φ k)
  obtain ⟨hcol⟩ := h0829 (J φ k) hJq
  let ℬ := SymSections.algebra (D.obj k)
  let R := (structurePresheaf B S hS F ⋙ forget₂ CommRingCat RingCat).obj (op U)
  let M := (SymSections.val' (D.obj k)).obj (op U)
  -- finitely many generators of the sections of `F_k` over `U`
  have hfinU : Module.Finite R M :=
    module_finite_sections_of_isFiniteTypeOnSite (D.obj k) (hD k)
      (SheafOfModules.isFiniteTypeOnSite_of_isFinitePresentationOnSite (D.obj k)) U hU
  obtain ⟨s, hs⟩ := hfinU.fg_top
  -- each generator satisfies a monic equation modulo a finite type submodule of `J_k`
  have key : ∀ m : (D.obj k).val.obj (op U),
      ∃ (E : FiniteTypeQuasicoherentSubobject B S hS F hF (J φ k))
        (p : Polynomial ((structureSheaf B S hS F hF).obj.obj (op U))) (_ : p.Monic)
        (z : (Subobject.underlying.obj E.obj).val.obj (op U)),
        (ι φ k).val.app (op U) (E.obj.arrow.val.app (op U) z) =
          p.eval₂ (ℬ.algebraMap (op U)) (SymSections.genApp (D.obj k) (op U) m) := by
    intro m
    obtain ⟨p, hpm, hp⟩ := hint U hU ((ψ φ k).right.hom.app (op U)
      (SymSections.genApp (D.obj k) (op U) m))
    have hw : (ψ φ k).right.hom.app (op U)
        (p.eval₂ (ℬ.algebraMap (op U)) (SymSections.genApp (D.obj k) (op U) m)) = 0 := by
      have h := Polynomial.hom_eval₂ p (ℬ.algebraMap (op U))
        ((ψ φ k).right.hom.app (op U)).hom (SymSections.genApp (D.obj k) (op U) m)
      rw [AlgebraSheaf.comp_algebraMap (ψ φ k) (op U)] at h
      exact h.trans hp
    let wJ : (J φ k).val.obj (op U) :=
      ⟨_, (SheafOfModules.mem_kerSubmodule _ _ _).2 hw⟩
    obtain ⟨E, z, hz⟩ := exists_eq_of_isColimit_of_mono
      (finiteTypeQuasicoherentSubobjectCocone B S hS F hF (J φ k)).ι hcol
      (fun E => (inferInstance : Mono E.obj.arrow)) hU wJ
    exact ⟨E, p, hpm, z, congrArg Subtype.val hz⟩
  choose Em pm hpm zm hzm using key
  -- an upper bound of `E` and the `E_m`
  let O : Finset (FiniteTypeQuasicoherentSubobject B S hS F hF (J φ k)) :=
    insert E₀ (s.image Em)
  let E' := IsFiltered.sup O ∅
  let j : Idx φ := ⟨k, E'⟩
  have hE₀ : E₀ ∈ O := Finset.mem_insert_self _ _
  have hEm : ∀ m ∈ s, Em m ∈ O := fun m hm =>
    Finset.mem_insert_of_mem (Finset.mem_image_of_mem _ hm)
  refine ⟨E', IsFiltered.toSup O ∅ hE₀, ?_⟩
  -- finiteness of `Sym(F_k)/(E')`, checked over `U`
  have hℬq : ℬ.IsQuasicoherent := SymSections.isQuasicoherent_algebra _ (hD k)
  refine AlgebraSheaf.isFinite_of_coversTop (isQuasicoherent_diagram_obj hD j) (fun _ => hU)
    hcov (fun _ => ?_)
  refine RingHom.finite_iff_isIntegral_and_finiteType.2
    ⟨?_, (isFinitePresentation_diagram_obj hD hD' j).isFiniteType U hU⟩
  have hcart := isCartesianOnAffineCharts_of_isQuasicoherentOnSite B S hS F hF (D.obj k) (hD k)
  have hbS := SymSections.bijective_unit_app (D.obj k) hcart U hU
  have hbQ := GenQuot.bijective_unit_app (n j) hℬq j.E.property.1 U hU
  let θ : SymmetricAlgebra R M →+* ((diagram φ).obj j).right.obj.obj (op U) :=
    ((GenQuot.unit (n j)).app (op U)).hom.comp
      ((GenQuot.mk (n j) (op U)).comp ((SymSections.unit (D.obj k)).app (op U)).hom)
  have hθ : Function.Surjective θ :=
    hbQ.2.comp (Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective.comp hbS.2)
  have heq : ((diagram φ).obj j).algebraMap (op U) =
      θ.comp (algebraMap R (SymmetricAlgebra R M)) := rfl
  rw [heq]
  refine SymmetricAlgebra.isIntegral_comp_algebraMap_of_surjective θ hθ (s : Set M) hs
    fun m hm => ⟨pm m, hpm m, ?_⟩
  refine (Polynomial.hom_eval₂ (pm m) _ θ _).symm.trans ?_
  have hle : (Em m).obj ≤ E'.obj := leOfHom (IsFiltered.toSup O ∅ (hEm m hm)).hom
  let z' := (Subobject.ofLE _ _ hle).val.app (op U) (zm m)
  have hz' : (n j).val.app (op U) z' =
      (pm m).eval₂ (ℬ.algebraMap (op U)) (SymSections.genApp (D.obj k) (op U) m) := by
    have h3 : Subobject.ofLE _ _ hle ≫ E'.obj.arrow ≫ ι φ k = (Em m).obj.arrow ≫ ι φ k := by
      rw [← Category.assoc, Subobject.ofLE_arrow]
    exact (ConcreteCategory.congr_hom (congrArg (fun g => g.val.app (op U)) h3) (zm m)).trans
      (hzm m)
  have hmk : GenQuot.mk (n j) (op U)
      ((pm m).eval₂ (ℬ.algebraMap (op U)) (SymSections.genApp (D.obj k) (op U) m)) = 0 :=
    Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem.2 (Ideal.subset_span ⟨z', hz'⟩)
  have hSym : ((SymSections.unit (D.obj k)).app (op U)).hom
      ((pm m).eval₂ (algebraMap R (SymmetricAlgebra R M)) (SymmetricAlgebra.ι R M m)) =
      (pm m).eval₂ (ℬ.algebraMap (op U)) (SymSections.genApp (D.obj k) (op U) m) :=
    Polynomial.hom_eval₂ _ _ _ _
  exact (congrArg (fun y => ((GenQuot.unit (n j)).app (op U)).hom (GenQuot.mk (n j) (op U) y))
    hSym).trans ((congrArg _ hmk).trans (map_zero _))

/-- The map of kernels `J_k ⟶ J_k` induced by the identity of `k` is the identity. -/
theorem jmap_id (k : K) : jmap φ (𝟙 k) = 𝟙 (J φ k) := by
  refine (cancel_mono (ι φ k)).1 ?_
  ext U z
  refine (ι_jmap_apply φ (𝟙 k) U z).trans ?_
  rw [D.map_id, SymSections.map_id]
  rfl

/-- **Every member of the system `(k, E) ↦ Sym(F_k)/(E)` maps to a finite one**, by
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.FPAlgColim.exists_le_isFinite` at the same `k`. -/
theorem exists_hom_isFinite (hfp : ∀ k, (D.obj k).IsFinitePresentation)
    (h𝒜 : 𝒜.IsQuasicoherent) (hint : 𝒜.IsIntegral)
    (h0829 : ∀ G : Modules.{u, u} B S hS F hF, G.IsQuasicoherentOnSite →
      Nonempty (IsColimit (finiteTypeQuasicoherentSubobjectCocone B S hS F hF G)))
    {U : SmallEtale B S hS F}
    (hU : IsAffine ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS F ⋙ BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj U))
    (hcov : (SmallEtale.topology B S hS F).CoversTop fun _ : PUnit.{u + 2} => U)
    (i : Idx φ) : ∃ (j : Idx φ) (_ : i ⟶ j), ((diagram φ).obj j).IsFinite := by
  obtain ⟨E, h, hE⟩ := exists_le_isFinite hfp h𝒜 hint h0829 hU hcov i.k i.E
  refine ⟨⟨i.k, E⟩, homOfImageLE (j := ⟨i.k, E⟩) (𝟙 i.k) ?_, hE⟩
  rw [jmap_id, Category.comp_id, imageSubobject_mono, Subobject.mk_arrow]
  exact leOfHom h.hom

end FPAlgColim

variable (B S hS F hF) in
/-- **An integral quasi-coherent algebra on a quasi-compact algebraic space is a directed colimit
of quasi-coherent algebras that are finite and of finite presentation**, given a filtered
presentation `φ` of its underlying module by modules of finite presentation and the colimit
assertion of Stacks 0829 on the space.  The index is a nonempty directed preorder in the universe
of the schemes, and the colimit is taken in the category of all algebra sheaves.

The finite members of the system `(k, E) ↦ Sym(F_k)/(E)` are cofinal in it
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.FPAlgColim.exists_hom_isFinite`), so the full subcategory they span is
filtered and its inclusion final, and the colimit of the system restricts to it; a directed
preorder then reindexes it. -/
theorem exists_directed_isColimit_isFinite_isFinitePresentation_of_presentation
    (hqc : IsQuasiCompactSpace B S hS F) (𝒜 : AlgebraSheaf.{u, u} B S hS F hF)
    (h𝒜 : 𝒜.IsQuasicoherent) (hint : 𝒜.IsIntegral) {K : Type u} [SmallCategory K] [IsFiltered K]
    {D : K ⥤ Modules.{u, u} B S hS F hF}
    (φ : D ⟶ (Functor.const K).obj (AlgebraSheaf.underlyingModule 𝒜))
    (hfp : ∀ k, (D.obj k).IsFinitePresentation) (hc : IsColimit (Cocone.mk _ φ))
    (h0829 : ∀ G : Modules.{u, u} B S hS F hF, G.IsQuasicoherentOnSite →
      Nonempty (IsColimit (finiteTypeQuasicoherentSubobjectCocone B S hS F hF G))) :
    ∃ (I : Type u) (_ : Preorder I) (_ : Nonempty I) (_ : IsDirected I (· ≤ ·))
      (E : I ⥤ AlgebraSheaf.{u, u} B S hS F hF) (t : E ⟶ (Functor.const I).obj 𝒜)
      (_ : IsColimit (Cocone.mk 𝒜 t)),
      ∀ i, (E.obj i).IsQuasicoherent ∧ (E.obj i).IsFinite ∧ (E.obj i).IsFinitePresentation := by
  obtain ⟨hD, hD'⟩ := FPAlgColim.isQuasicoherentOnSite_and_isFinitePresentationOnSite hfp
  obtain ⟨U, hU, hcov⟩ := SmallEtale.exists_affineObject_coversTop B S hS F hF hqc
  have := FPAlgColim.isFiltered hD h𝒜 (φ := φ)
  have := FPAlgColim.essentiallySmall (φ := φ)
  obtain ⟨hcol⟩ := FPAlgColim.nonempty_isColimit hc hD h𝒜 h0829
  let P : ObjectProperty (FPAlgColim.Idx φ) := fun j => ((FPAlgColim.diagram φ).obj j).IsFinite
  have hP : ∀ i, ∃ j : P.FullSubcategory, Nonempty (i ⟶ P.ι.obj j) := fun i => by
    obtain ⟨j, f, hj⟩ := FPAlgColim.exists_hom_isFinite hfp h𝒜 hint h0829 hU hcov i
    exact ⟨⟨j, hj⟩, ⟨f⟩⟩
  have : IsFiltered P.FullSubcategory := IsFiltered.of_exists_of_isFiltered_of_fullyFaithful P.ι hP
  have : P.ι.Final := Functor.final_of_exists_of_isFiltered_of_fullyFaithful P.ι hP
  have : EssentiallySmall.{u} P.FullSubcategory := essentiallySmall_of_fully_faithful P.ι
  have hcolP : IsColimit (Cocone.mk 𝒜 (Functor.whiskerLeft P.ι (FPAlgColim.coconeι φ))) :=
    (Functor.Final.isColimitWhiskerEquiv P.ι (Cocone.mk 𝒜 (FPAlgColim.coconeι φ))).symm hcol
  exact Stacks.FilteredCardIndex.exists_directed_index_of_isFiltered.{u}
    (Functor.whiskerLeft P.ι (FPAlgColim.coconeι φ)) hcolP
    (fun A : AlgebraSheaf.{u, u} B S hS F hF =>
      A.IsQuasicoherent ∧ A.IsFinite ∧ A.IsFinitePresentation)
    (fun j => ⟨FPAlgColim.isQuasicoherent_diagram_obj hD j.obj, j.property,
      FPAlgColim.isFinitePresentation_diagram_obj hD hD' j.obj⟩)

variable (B S hS) in
/-- **Both clauses of Stacks 082C on a quasi-compact and quasi-separated algebraic space whose
quasi-coherent modules are filtered colimits of modules of finite presentation** — which is the
conclusion of Stacks 07V9, the hypothesis `h07V9` here.  For an integral quasi-coherent algebra
`A`:

1. the finite quasi-coherent subalgebras of `A` form a filtered category and `A` is the colimit of
   the cocone of their inclusions, and
2. `A` is the colimit of a directed system, over a nonempty directed preorder in the universe of
   the schemes, of quasi-coherent algebras that are finite and of finite presentation.

The colimit assertion of Stacks 0829, which clause (2) uses on the kernels `J_k`, is derived from
`h07V9` by `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isColimit_finiteTypeQuasicoherentSubobjectCocone_of_07V9`. -/
theorem isFiltered_isColimit_finiteSubalgebra_and_exists_directed_finite_of_presentation
    (Y : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS) (hqc : IsQuasiCompactSpace B S hS Y.1)
    (hqs : IsAbsolutelyQuasiSeparated B S hS B.contains_terminal Y.1)
    (h07V9 : ∀ G : Modules.{u, u} B S hS Y.1 Y.2, G.IsQuasicoherentOnSite →
      ∃ (K : Type u) (inst : SmallCategory K),
        let _ := inst
        ∃ (_ : IsFiltered K) (D : K ⥤ Modules.{u, u} B S hS Y.1 Y.2)
          (φ : D ⟶ (Functor.const K).obj G),
          (∀ k, (D.obj k).IsFinitePresentation) ∧ Nonempty (IsColimit (Cocone.mk G φ)))
    (A : AlgebraSheaf.{u, u} B S hS Y.1 Y.2) (hA : A.IsQuasicoherent) (hint : A.IsIntegral) :
    (IsFiltered (FiniteSubalgebra B S hS Y.1 Y.2 A) ∧
        Nonempty (IsColimit (finiteSubalgebraCocone B S hS Y.1 Y.2 A))) ∧
      ∃ (I : Type u) (_ : Preorder I) (_ : Nonempty I) (_ : IsDirected I (· ≤ ·))
        (D : I ⥤ AlgebraSheaf.{u, u} B S hS Y.1 Y.2) (t : D ⟶ (Functor.const I).obj A)
        (_ : IsColimit (Cocone.mk A t)),
